            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R1-001",
                "lens": "risk",
                "location": "engine/review/fsstore/fsstore.go:121-142",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "walk checks each directory with Lstat and then uses it in a separate call, so a symlink swapped in between is not detected (TOCTOU). The package documentation states this limit explicitly, and exploiting it requires a process that can already write to the working tree, so no reachable impact beyond that exists.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/review/fsstore/fsstore.go:20-23"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths in full.",
              "Feature and name inputs are validated before any filesystem access: review.CheckFeature for the feature, checkName for the file name (rejects empty, dot names, a leading dot, separators, backslash, NUL, and names over 255 bytes).",
              "Every directory on the way from the root is Lstat-checked and refused if it is a symlink or not a directory, so the intended threat of a symlink brought in by a checked-out branch is blocked. Tests cover links at odd, review-results and the feature directory.",
              "Create publishes through atomicfile Stage plus Create (link semantics), so an existing file is never overwritten and a dangling symlink at the name counts as taken. The tests cover both cases and the race between writers.",
              "Directory and file modes are fixed at 0755 and 0644 regardless of umask. They are world-readable by design, since the results are evidence read by other users of the checkout, and contain no secrets.",
              "No dependencies were added and no secrets appear in the patch. The architecture_test.go change only registers the new package as an Adapter ring."
            ]
          }
        }
