            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Create stages into a temp file in the same directory, syncs it, and links it to its name through atomicfile. A crash leaves no half-written result, and a taken name, including a dangling symlink, maps to app.ErrExists and is left untouched. The tests cover this.",
              "staged.Discard is deferred, so a failed Create leaves no temporary file behind. TestCreateFailsWhenTheDirectoryCannotBeWritten covers a non-writable directory.",
              "walk uses Lstat on each directory, refuses symlinks and non-directories, and makeDir handles a concurrent mkdir by re-inspecting the directory. The residual check-then-use race is documented in the package comment and is not a regression, since this is new code with no baseline behavior.",
              "Names does not create anything. A missing directory returns an empty result without error, so reads degrade gracefully.",
              "The new code is isolated, adds no retry loops or unbounded work, and has no concrete production failure mode. I found no resilience defects caused by this candidate."
            ]
          }
        }
